  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Request:\n\nPlease allocate more of the camera zoom bar to zooming out.  Right now it's about 90/10 zoom in/zoom out.  Please change this to something like 80/20 for better control of zoom out with minimal impact to zoom in control.  See attached sketch.\n\nLonger Explanation:\n\nControlling zoom on the VRC camera is done by clicking a bar on the right hand side of the camera screen.  Currently ~90% of this bar is dedicated to zooming in which provides extremely fine control of zoom level in the zoom in direction.  The other ~10% of the bar is dedicated to zooming out which is so small it makes it very difficult to accurately zoom the camera out, especially given how much zoom out capability the camera has.  \n\nI prefer to use a zoom level that is zoomed out from the default zoom level for all of my Twitch streams and I always have to click 3-4 times to try to get the zoom out level set to something I'm happy with.  This causes rapid changes to zoom level which looks bad on stream as I have to fiddle with it due to how small the zoom out bar is.\n\nIf there was more space available on the zoom out bar it would be much easier to select the zoom out level.",
